  "description": "config.yaml's worker.open_timeout (V7): the bound on a shell's open, how long the worker waits for the target to open a shell, sent on C3 open_shell as open_timeout to a worker at proto_version 0.6 or later; a target's own options.open_timeout overrides it. A Go duration string, as its siblings undialled_timeout and reap_timeout, and optional in this schema as every later knob is. Each instance is config-valid's lab template with only worker.open_timeout varied. Valid: 20s; absent. Invalid: a non-duration string; a negative duration. The lower bound is prose, as the loader enforces it: 0s and a fractional-millisecond 1.5ms match the schema's pattern, so they validate here and are listed as the loader's refusal cases, which only U5's loader test grades. The default is config.yaml's, never this schema's (decision 5.36).",
  "corpus": [
    "Storage §2.5",
    "session model §11",
    "decision 5.36",
    "lang-arch §7.3"
  ],
